text:
Elena K: quick accessibility note from today's UI pass — the collapsible side panel (dark theme) focus outline barely shows when a panel is expanded.
Devon (UX): yeah saw that. the panel header uses a 1px border for focus and it disappears against #0c1116.
Ruth - Eng: current markup: <div role="region" aria-labelledby="panel-1-heading"> with the toggle as a plain button. We need to ensure aria-expanded toggles and the focus style is visible.
Carlos (QA): VoiceOver reads the label fine but doesn't announce expansion reliably sometimes. Could be timing with animation.
Elena K: two problems then: contrast/visibility of focus + SR announce on expand/collapse. Proposed CSS focus change: 
```css
.panel-toggle:focus-visible {
  outline: none;
  box-shadow: 0 0 0 3px rgba(255, 200, 120, 0.12), 0 0 0 2px #ffd58a; /* warm halo */
  border-radius: 6px;
}
```
That gives a thicker, warmer halo that reads against dark bg. Aim for min 3:1 against #0c1116.
Devon (UX): warm halo works with brand palette. Also let's increase hit target on the toggle to 28px.
Ruth - Eng: will do. For SR announce: ensure the toggle button has aria-expanded and the panel has aria-hidden toggled during animation end. Avoid announcing mid-animation. Add `aria-live="polite"` on a hidden announcer that updates to "Panel \u2014 {name} expanded" after transitionend.
Carlos (QA): test suggestion: Playwright should assert aria-expanded toggles and the announcer receives text after transitionend. Also validate focus remains on the toggle after expansion so keyboard users don't get lost.
Elena K: edge case: nested interactive elements inside the panel. When collapsed, inner items should be inert/unfocusable. Use inert polyfill or set tabindex=-1 on inner controls when panel is collapsed.
Ruth - Eng: good call. We'll toggle `inert` where available and fallback to `aria-hidden=true` + tabindex management.
Devon (UX): semantic nit: consider role="region" with aria-labelledby pointing to the header so SR users know context. Don't rely on heading text alone.
Carlos (QA): automation: add axe check to CI to catch color-contrast and also a test that tabs to the toggle, presses Enter, waits for transitionend, asserts announcer text includes "expanded" and that first inner control is not tabbable when collapsed.
A11yBot: automated scan (panel component): 1 major (focus contrast low), 2 minor (missing inert on collapsed content, missing aria-live updates). Scanned 47 nodes.
Ruth - Eng: implementation plan:
- add focus token + CSS change (D: 1 day)
- implement aria-expanded + aria-hidden sync + transitionend announcer (D: 1 day)
- inert/tabindex fallback for inner elements (D: 2 days)
- QA Playwright + axe tests (Carlos D: 2 days)
Devon (UX): I'll update the component spec in Figma and note the focus size + hit target.
Elena K: quick code example for announcer: 
```js
toggleButton.addEventListener('click', () => {
  const expanded = toggleButton.getAttribute('aria-expanded') === 'true';
  toggleButton.setAttribute('aria-expanded', String(!expanded));
  panel.classList.toggle('is-collapsed');
});
panel.addEventListener('transitionend', (e) => {
  if (e.propertyName !== 'height') return;
  const announcer = document.getElementById('panel-announcer');
  announcer.textContent = panel.classList.contains('is-collapsed') ? `${panelName} collapsed` : `${panelName} expanded`;
});
```
Carlos (QA): that'll help. Also watch screen reader verbosity; keep messages concise: "Logs panel expanded" rather than long descriptions.
Ruth - Eng: will open PR with small CSS + JS tweaks. If it's just tokens + aria attr updates it should be a patch release.
Elena K: priority P2. escalate if any customer reports. Thanks all.
A11yBot: reminder: save test traces to /tests/fixtures/panel-a11y-failures.json
Carlos (QA): will post failing Playwright run if it crops up. :white_check_mark:
